IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eca-nouns`
IMPORT `eca-schedules`
IMPORT `eca-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `eca-part3-appeals`

-- Tests of Part 3, Division 4 and section 27 (ss 23 to 27).  Every expected value was decided from the text before the run and is written beside its assertion.

§ `Tests -- s 23`

#ASSERT `s 23(2) the condition that a District Court gives permission to appeal is met` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the condition that a District Court gives permission to appeal is met` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 23(1): args = party to the proceedings, order under s 22(1), ground
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` TRUE TRUE `A ground involving a question of law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` TRUE TRUE `That the claim was outside the jurisdiction of the tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` TRUE TRUE `A question of fact` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` TRUE TRUE `Another ground` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` FALSE TRUE `A ground involving a question of law` EQUALS NOTHING  -- not a party
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` TRUE FALSE `A ground involving a question of law` EQUALS NOTHING  -- not an order under s 22(1)
-- s 23(1) and (2)
#ASSERT `s 23(1) and (2) an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) and (2) an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- no permission
#ASSERT `s 23(1) and (2) an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- no permission whatever the ground
#ASSERT `s 23(1) and (2) an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1) and (2) an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(a) a District Court may extend the time under section 22(10) for the correction of the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(a) a District Court may extend the time under section 22(10) for the correction of the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(b) a District Court may remit the matter to a tribunal for the correction of the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(3)(b) a District Court may remit the matter to a tribunal for the correction of the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the order is final and is not subject to any appeal` `An order giving or refusing permission under section 23(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the order is final and is not subject to any appeal` `An order extending or refusing to extend under section 23(3)(a) the time under section 22(10)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the order is final and is not subject to any appeal` `An order remitting or refusing to remit under section 23(3)(b) a matter to a tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the order is final and is not subject to any appeal` `Another order` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 24`

#ASSERT `s 24(1) the appeal by itself operates as a stay of execution or enforcement of the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(1) the appeal by itself operates as a stay of execution or enforcement of the order` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the court may direct that a stay be subject to any conditions it thinks fit` `The General Division of the High Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the court may direct that a stay be subject to any conditions it thinks fit` `A District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the court may direct that a stay be subject to any conditions it thinks fit` `A Magistrate's Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the court may direct that a stay be subject to any conditions it thinks fit` `Another court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the order or direction is final and is not subject to any appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(3) the order or direction is final and is not subject to any appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(4): args = permission given under s 23(2), an application for a stay was made to a District Court
#ASSERT `s 24(4) the conditions for the General Division of the High Court to order a stay are met` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(4) the conditions for the General Division of the High Court to order a stay are met` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(4) the conditions for the General Division of the High Court to order a stay are met` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24(4) the conditions for the General Division of the High Court to order a stay are met` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 25`

#ASSERT `s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` `Dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` `Allow the appeal and set aside or vary the order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` `Remit the matter to the tribunal for reconsideration, or order a rehearing by a different tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` `Make any other order, including an order as to costs and expenses` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` `Reverse or vary a determination made by a tribunal on a question of fact` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` `Receive further evidence` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` `Some other step` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the General Division of the High Court may take into account the tripartite guidelines on re-employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(3) the General Division of the High Court may take into account the tripartite guidelines on re-employment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25(4)(a) the General Division of the High Court is to have regard to the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(4)(a) the General Division of the High Court is to have regard to the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25(4)(b) the General Division of the High Court is to calculate the compensation in accordance with the regulations made under section 34(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25(4)(b) the General Division of the High Court is to calculate the compensation in accordance with the regulations made under section 34(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25(4)(b) the General Division of the High Court is to calculate the compensation in accordance with the regulations made under section 34(1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- ss 26 and 27`

#ASSERT `s 26 the judgment, order or direction of the General Division of the High Court is final` `An appeal against an order made by a tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26 the judgment, order or direction of the General Division of the High Court is final` `An application for a stay of execution or enforcement of an order made by a tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26 the judgment, order or direction of the General Division of the High Court is final` `Another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the person who makes the allegation bears the burden of proving it` TRUE `That the person is not the employer or employee of the claimant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the person who makes the allegation bears the burden of proving it` TRUE `That the person is not a person who has a duty under the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001, the Employment Act 1968 or the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the person who makes the allegation bears the burden of proving it` TRUE `Another allegation` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the person who makes the allegation bears the burden of proving it` FALSE `That the person is not the employer or employee of the claimant` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(a) the employer bears the burden of proving that the employee was dismissed with just cause or excuse` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(a) the employer bears the burden of proving that the employee was dismissed with just cause or excuse` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(a) the employer bears the burden of proving that the employee was dismissed with just cause or excuse` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(a) the employer bears the burden of proving that the employee was dismissed with just cause or excuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(b) the employer bears the burden of proving the ground for giving the notice of dismissal` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(b) the employer bears the burden of proving the ground for giving the notice of dismissal` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(b) the employer bears the burden of proving the ground for giving the notice of dismissal` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(b) the employer bears the burden of proving the ground for giving the notice of dismissal` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(c) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee was dismissed with sufficient cause` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(c) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee was dismissed with sufficient cause` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(c) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee was dismissed with sufficient cause` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(c) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee was dismissed with sufficient cause` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(d) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 was dismissed with sufficient cause` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(d) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 was dismissed with sufficient cause` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(d) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 was dismissed with sufficient cause` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(d) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 was dismissed with sufficient cause` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- the rulings of 2026-11-05 and the review's findings`

-- s 24(1), the other half: execution is stayed pending an appeal where a court orders a stay.  args = an appeal has been brought, a court orders a stay
#ASSERT `s 24(1) execution or enforcement of the order is stayed pending the appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(1) execution or enforcement of the order is stayed pending the appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- "does not operate as a stay"
#ASSERT `s 24(1) execution or enforcement of the order is stayed pending the appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING  -- no appeal: the clause is not spoken to
-- s 27(2): the proceedings are a scope (ruled I(c)); the "where" in each paragraph is a condition (ruled I(b))
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(a) the employer bears the burden of proving that the employee was dismissed with just cause or excuse` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court
#ASSERT `s 27(2)(b) the employer bears the burden of proving the ground for giving the notice of dismissal` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 23(1): the appeal is to the General Division of the High Court
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the court is the one to which the party may appeal` `The General Division of the High Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the court is the one to which the party may appeal` `A District Court` EQUALS NOTHING  -- a District Court gives or refuses permission (s 23(2)); the appeal itself is not to it
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the court is the one to which the party may appeal` `Another court` EQUALS NOTHING
